Origin
------
This work was produced in the context of the 6GoASIS research project at
Nearby Computing, and released by Nearby Computing under Apache-2.0 as a
project deliverable. The copyright holder is Nearby Computing S.L.; the
author of the work in this repository is Michail Dalgitsis.

Publications
------------
The offline studies in studies/ are the evaluation behind:

  M. Dalgitsis, G. M. Kibalya, M. A. Serrano, J. Serra and A. Antonopoulos,
  "Exploiting 6G RAN and Core Network Information for Intelligent Edge-Cloud
  Service Orchestration," 2025 Joint European Conference on Networks and
  Communications & 6G Summit (EuCNC/6G Summit), Poznan, Poland, 2025,
  pp. 369-374. doi: 10.1109/EuCNC/6GSummit63408.2025.11037032

The closed-loop approach this repository implements is also one of the use
cases in:

  M. Dalgitsis, E. Datsika, C. Santana Casillas and A. Antonopoulos,
  "6G-Core-in-the-Loop: Enabling Service and Network Orchestration in a
  Cloud-Native Ecosystem," IEEE Communications Standards Magazine, vol. 10,
  no. 2, pp. 72-79, June 2026. doi: 10.1109/MCOMSTD.2026.3657234

Scope
-----
The original deployment realised the scaling algorithm inside a separate
commercial orchestration platform. That platform is proprietary and out of
scope here; the controller in autoscaler/ is an independent implementation of
the published algorithm, written against Prometheus and the Kubernetes API
alone.

Third-party
-----------
The operator is scaffolded with Kubebuilder (Apache-2.0) and uses
confluent-kafka-go (Apache-2.0).
